BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir East Sicily//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:East Sicily — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Granita di mandorla con brioche — Almond ice\, coarse-grained\, with a warm brioche col tuppo.
DESCRIPTION:Say: gra-NEE-ta dee man-DOR-la. Breakfast on this coast\, all year. The ice once came down from Etna's snow pits. Best: Caffè Sicilia\, Noto — at opening
LOCATION:Caffè Sicilia\, Noto — at opening
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Caff%C3%A8+Sicilia+Noto+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Arancino al ragù — Fried rice cone filled with meat ragù and peas.
DESCRIPTION:Say: a-ran-CHEE-no. In Catania it is masculine and pointed\; in Palermo it is arancina and round. The Accademia della Crusca accepts both. Best: Pasticceria Savia\, Via Etnea\, Catania
LOCATION:Pasticceria Savia\, Via Etnea\, Catania
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pasticceria+Savia+Catania+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pasta alla Norma — Pasta with fried aubergine\, tomato\, salted ricotta and basil.
DESCRIPTION:Say: PAS-ta al-la NOR-ma. Catania's dish\; the name is either Bellini's opera or a playwright's 'a true Norma' — neither documented at the time. Best: Me Cumpari Turiddu\, Catania
LOCATION:Me Cumpari Turiddu\, Catania
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Me+Cumpari+Turiddu+Catania+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cipollina — Puff pastry round with onion\, ham\, tomato and cheese.
DESCRIPTION:Say: chee-pol-LEE-na. A rosticceria piece found almost only in Catania. Best: Pasticceria Savia or Spinella\, Via Etnea\, Catania
LOCATION:Pasticceria Savia or Spinella\, Via Etnea\, Catania
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pasticceria+Spinella+Catania+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Seltz limone e sale — Fresh lemon squeezed into soda water with a pinch of salt.
DESCRIPTION:Say: SELTS lee-MO-ne eh SA-le. Catania's kiosk drink\, for heat and for the morning after. Best: Chiosco Giammona\, Piazza Umberto\, Catania (unverified)
LOCATION:Chiosco Giammona\, Piazza Umberto\, Catania (unverified)
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Chiosco+Giammona+Catania+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Arrusti e mancia — 'Roast and eat' — horse meat grilled on the street.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ar-ROOS-tee eh MAN-cha. The Via Plebiscito grills are a Catanese institution\; a national bill to ban horse meat was in committee in 2026. Best: Canusciuti\, Catania — the Plebiscito sandwich
LOCATION:Canusciuti\, Catania — the Plebiscito sandwich
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Canusciuti+Catania+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Crudo di gambero rosso — Raw red prawns\, from the stalls outside.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KROO-do. The Pescheria is a few steps away\; eat it at the room that buys from it. Best: Osteria Antica Marina\, Catania (Pescheria)
LOCATION:Osteria Antica Marina\, Catania (Pescheria)
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Osteria+Antica+Marina+Catania+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Panino di Borderi — A sandwich built to order with the house's own cheeses.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pa-NEE-no. The Ortigia market's most famous queue. Unverified for 2026 — check before you plan the morning on it. Best: Caseificio Borderi\, Ortigia market
LOCATION:Caseificio Borderi\, Ortigia market
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Caseificio+Borderi+Ortigia+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Busiate con bottarga di tonno — Twisted pasta with grated dried tuna roe.
DESCRIPTION:Say: boo-zee-AH-te con bot-TAR-ga. Marzamemi's tonnara is gone\; the tuna still comes home as bottarga. Best: Campisi\, Marzamemi
LOCATION:Campisi\, Marzamemi
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Campisi+Marzamemi+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cannolo and cassata — Fried shell with ricotta\; the baroque ricotta cake.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kan-NO-lo · kas-SA-ta. Convent pastry\, pared back at Caffè Sicilia by Corrado Assenza\, who subtracts sugar rather than adds it. Best: Caffè Sicilia\, Noto
LOCATION:Caffè Sicilia\, Noto
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Caff%C3%A8+Sicilia+Noto+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cioccolato di Modica — Chocolate worked cold\, gritty with sugar crystals.
DESCRIPTION:Say: chok-ko-LA-to dee MO-dee-ka. Cioccolato di Modica IGP since 2018\; Bonajuto\, the oldest maker (1880)\, left the consortium and sells it under its own name. Best: Antica Dolceria Bonajuto\, Modica
LOCATION:Antica Dolceria Bonajuto\, Modica
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Antica+Dolceria+Bonajuto+Modica+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:'Mpanatigghi — Crescent pastries of minced beef\, chocolate\, almond and spice.
DESCRIPTION:Say: m-pa-na-TEEG-ghee. Meat and chocolate in one sweet\; the name is usually traced to Spanish empanadas. Best: Antica Dolceria Bonajuto\, Modica
LOCATION:Antica Dolceria Bonajuto\, Modica
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Antica+Dolceria+Bonajuto+Modica+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cremolata — Modica's granita: fruit-heavy\, creamier\, with nuts.
DESCRIPTION:Say: kre-mo-LA-ta. The fig one with walnut and Modica chocolate is the town's own. Best: Rosy Bar\, Modica
LOCATION:Rosy Bar\, Modica
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Rosy+Bar+Modica+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Minne di Sant'Agata — Small iced ricotta cassatas topped with a cherry.
DESCRIPTION:Say: MEEN-ne dee sant-A-ga-ta. Shaped for the saint's martyrdom in 251\; made for February\, sold year-round at Savia. Best: Pasticceria Savia\, Catania
LOCATION:Pasticceria Savia\, Catania
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Pasticceria+Savia+Catania+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Granita al pistacchio — Pistachio granita\, the indulgent order.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pee-STAK-kyo. The Bronte pistachio is a DOP grown on lava and harvested only in odd years. Best: Bar Alecci\, Gravina di Catania
LOCATION:Bar Alecci\, Gravina di Catania
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Bar+Alecci+Gravina+di+Catania+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-16@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Etna Rosso di contrada — Nerello Mascalese bottled by its named lava parcel.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ET-na ROS-so. The mountain's red: high\, pale\, tannic\, the most talked-about new wine in Italy. Best: A booked tasting at Graci\, Castiglione di Sicilia
LOCATION:A booked tasting at Graci\, Castiglione di Sicilia
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Graci+Castiglione+di+Sicilia+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-17@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Etna Bianco Superiore — Carricante from the commune of Milo.
DESCRIPTION:Say: BYAN-ko soo-pe-RYO-re. Only Milo may call its Etna white Superiore\; it ages like few southern whites. Best: Benanti\, Viagrande — Pietra Marina
LOCATION:Benanti\, Viagrande — Pietra Marina
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Benanti+Viagrande+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-18@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Moscato di Siracusa — The sweet white of Siracusa\, revived.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mos-KA-to. Siracusa's sweet wine was nearly lost\; Pupillo brought it back. Best: Cantine Pupillo\, Siracusa
LOCATION:Cantine Pupillo\, Siracusa
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Cantine+Pupillo+Siracusa+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-19@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Cerasuolo di Vittoria — Nero d'Avola and Frappato\, light-red and cherry-scented.
DESCRIPTION:Say: che-ra-SWO-lo dee vit-TOR-ya. Sicily's only DOCG\; COS makes some of it in clay amphorae. Best: COS\, Vittoria
LOCATION:COS\, Vittoria
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=COS+Vittoria+Sicilia
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:east-sicily-liste-20@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Vino alla mandorla — Sweet almond wine\, served cold.
DESCRIPTION:Say: VEE-no al-la MAN-dor-la. Castelmola's own drink\, at the café on the square above Taormina. Best: Antico Caffè San Giorgio\, Castelmola (unverified)
LOCATION:Antico Caffè San Giorgio\, Castelmola (unverified)
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Antico+Caff%C3%A8+San+Giorgio+Castelmola+Sicilia
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
